Body:
While you wait for native DuckDuckGo support, you can drop in a DuckDuckGo-based MCP server as an external tool right now — no API key required:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "web-search": {
      "command": "npx",
      "args": ["-y", "@tiagohanna/web-search-mcp"]
    }
  }
}
```

This is the [Web Search MCP Server](https://github.com/tiagohanna/web-search-mcp) — it runs purely on DuckDuckGo so there are zero paid API keys involved. Free tier gives 7 requests/IP/day, and fetch_url is included for full page content. Pro tier is R$50/year (≈$9 USD) if you need unlimited.

Correction on the npx command above — the package is not on npm yet. The correct way to run it is via git clone:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/tiagohanna123/agent-web-search-mcp
cd agent-web-search-mcp
npm install
PORT=3169 node index.js
```

Then add to your MCP config:
```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "web-search": {
      "command": "node",
      "args": ["path/to/agent-web-search-mcp/index.js"],
      "env": {"PORT": "3169"}
    }
  }
}
```

The repo is [tiagohanna123/agent-web-search-mcp](https://github.com/tiagohanna123/agent-web-search-mcp).

> The plugin is now working fine with the npm package instead of the GitHub install. And auto model works even after hitting 5h or weekly rate limits.
> 
> See https://github.com/m0wer/opencode-github-copilot-auto-model for the new install instructions.

So I put this in my `opencode.jsonc` file

```
"plugin": [
    [
      "opencode-github-copilot-auto-model",
      {
        "autos": [
          {
            "preferredModels": ["claude-sonnet-4.6", "claude-haiku-4.5"],
          },
          {
            "name": "Auto GPT/Codex",
            "preferredModels": ["gpt-5.4", "gpt-5.4-mini"],
          },
          {
            // Limited/best-effort: see "Gemini and other non-session models".
            "name": "Auto Gemini",
            "preferredModels": ["gemini-3.1-pro-preview", "gemini-3.5-flash"],
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
  ],
```

I'm able to see these options in the models list 
- Auto
- Auto Claude
- Auto GPT/Codex
- Auto Gemini

No matter which one I chose, I'm still getting the error model is not supported. One thing I noticed is that if I start a new session with the Auto model, I saw briefly the notification stating a model like GPT 5.4 and reasoning something before this error appears.

